  "body": "### Summary\n\nAs the maintainer, I want one **Fable** audit of every lot delivered by an outside contributor before the release gate, so that work reviewed only by the contributor's own agents gets a second, independent look before SwiftHFR ships.\n\n### On hold\n\nHeld by the operator's schedule (decision of 2026-10-29, this issue's \"When\"): the audit runs after every other lot of the M4 board (#324) and before LOT-164 (#254). ([decision](https://github.com/ezzz/HFRnow/issues/326))\n\n\n### Why\n\nUnder the operator decision of 2026-10-29, outside contributors may have their adversarial review done by another of their own agents. The model matrix still applies: the reviewer is never the author model. A different person is not required. That keeps throughput up, but the author and the reviewer share one operator, so this issue adds a final independent audit.\n\n**Outside contributor** means any claim or PR author other than the maintainer's own sessions: Bybifok (`moust4ki`), Ezzz's agents, or anyone else (`ext/<name>-…` ids). The steward session `ext/opus-helper1` acts for the maintainer and does not count.\n\n### Scope: the list to audit\n\nThe steward or orchestrator appends a line here when such a PR merges: `#PR (LOT-XXX or #issue) — author id — reviewer id/model — merged as <sha>`.\n\n- [ ] #319 (#314, flag writes only in a confirmed session) — `moust4ki` (Opus) — reviewed by Fable (cross-contributor) — merged as 7366c56\n\n### When\n\nAlmost last: after every other lot of the M4 board (#324), and **before LOT-164 (#254), the legacy parity gate**, which waits on this issue. It stays `status: blocked` until then.\n\n### How\n\n- A fresh **Fable** session gets the merged diff of each listed PR, its issue (acceptance criteria), AGENTS.md, LESSONS.md, ARCHITECTURE.md and HFR-PROTOCOL.md, and the current code around it. It does not get the PR discussion.\n- It returns, per PR: OK, or numbered findings (severity, file:line, failing scenario, fix).\n- High and Medium findings become fix issues. Security findings go to the maintainer privately (SECURITY.md).\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] Every PR in the list has a Fable verdict posted here.\n- [ ] Every High or Medium finding has its own issue, or a recorded operator decision.\n- [ ] LOT-164 starts only after this issue is closed.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
